      "problem": "Find the domain of the function $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{x+y}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that\n\n- $\\sqrt{x+y}$ is defined for $x$ and $y,$ such that $x+y\\ge 0,$ and\n\n- $\\operatorname{cos}⁡g(x,y)$ is defined if $g(x,y)$ is defined.\n\nAs a result, $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{x+y}$ is defined for values of $x$ and $y$ that satisfy $x+y\\ge 0.$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $f$ is\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x+y\\ge 0\\}.\n$$",
